## Context

The reopened 0515 (PR #930) confirmed RAG **equalisation** on the four-agent
Exp 2 cohort (Anthropic/Mistral/OpenAI/Qwen) using existing data — no new API
runs. The ticket *title* also named four out-of-cohort models — Sonnet, Mistral
Medium, Mistral Small, DeepSeek — whose arm-1D points would extend the
equalisation evidence to a wider model set. Those runs were deferred (the prior
CUT's probe outputs did not survive, and 0515 was scoped to existing data).
This ticket tracks the deferred extension so it is not silently lost.

## What to do

1. Run Exp2 arm 1D (RAG + deterministic doc set) on the four models. Apply the
   journal-backlog fixes the prior CUT documented:
   - **served-DeepSeek selection** (v3.2 retired from OpenRouter; pick a served
     endpoint, and use OpenRouter's `reasoning:` disable field — the harness
     `extra_body.think=false` was ignored by the DeepSeek backend).
   - **canonicalizer support for bilingual / link-formatted source columns**
     (Mistral Small output was unscoreable).
   - DeepSeek is MoE → `repeat=3` mandatory.
2. Test-one-before-blasting (mandatory): dry-run, one real call per model,
   inspect tokens/cost/content, then batch.
3. Score via the existing arm-3 path; compute delta arm0→arm1D per model.
4. If the new points support equalisation, fold them into the §6 observation
   (numbers from the generated CSV, adherence-guarded) and consider an F1 panel
   on the Exp 2 figure (it currently plots coverage/cost, not F1).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Four models run on arm 1D (DeepSeek repeat=3), within budget
- [ ] Delta arm0→arm1D scored; equalisation evaluated for the extended set
- [ ] §6 updated if supported (CSV-derived, adherence-guarded), else documented
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Related

0515 (the four-agent equalisation, closed via PR #930); 0508 perimeter.
This is journal-version work (new API spend) — not in the arXiv critical path.
